            <ArticleTitle>Effects of bepridil on the resting electrocardiogram.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We evaluated the effects of bepridil hydrochloride, a long-acting calcium antagonist, on the electrocardiogram of 13 men with exertional angina. The drug decreased sinus rate (P = 0.01), increased the QT (P less than 0.001) and QTc interval (P less than 0.001), and produced T-wave changes in each patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
